        "statement": "In the retained client-change execution the committed membership was rewritten without the replaced configuration's majority: the leader had reconstructed one voter against the three voters recorded at log index 106 in its own log, its client AddVoter with prevIndex 0 completed (change_committed true), and its configuration afterwards had two voters — itself and the fresh instance, which was not part of the replaced configuration — with the two peers that had held votes there carried as nonvoters. Both of those peers, restarted with the flag disabled, adopted the rewritten configuration (demoted_peers_adopted 2) and held no vote in it (demoted_peers_with_vote 0), while with the flag disabled the same node could not be leader with the others down, the change failed with \"node is not the leader\" and both peers kept their votes.",
